# Pinned llama.cpp engine — the build BOTH installers bundle.
#
# Moved here from installer-linux/ in 1.7.4. It was only ever read by the deb
# build, and the Windows installer had no pin at all: it bundled whatever
# happened to be sitting in installer/vendor/, with a heuristic look for
# ggml-vulkan.dll as the only check. That meant the .exe and the .deb carrying
# the same version number could contain different engines, and nothing anywhere
# recorded which. A shared pin at the repo root is the same rule VERSION
# already follows — one literal, read by every builder.
#
# Bumping LLAMA_BUILD means updating every hash below in the same commit. That
# is the point of pinning: a deliberate change, not a silent fetch of whatever
# upstream published this morning.
#
# Verified against https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/tag/b10456
#
# Asset naming differs per platform and is not guessable from one to the other:
# Linux archives are .tar.gz and the CPU one is "-bin-ubuntu-x64" rather than
# "-bin-ubuntu-cpu-x64"; the Windows archive is .zip and "-bin-win-vulkan-x64".
LLAMA_BUILD=b10456

# Linux (installer-linux/build-deb.sh)
GPU_SHA256=856fcfe9b273e6e813c8d5745396693080ce1cca8134b1180f0e8e2f22b21772
CPU_SHA256=d07b3f80f3a1ed1de46bfba5671b4af40a87417e1dbf35d0603ad2d623ddc577

# Windows (`gobbonet engine install`; launch.bat carries its own pin)
# llama-b10456-bin-win-vulkan-x64.zip
WIN_GPU_SHA256=60f3d31cc7c2fe62de8f34f8d75ffd06655b4de83bcc5aa6f08df56be42ebb91

# OpenSSL 3 for the AppImage and the ZIP (1.8.1; scripts/fetch-openssl3.sh).
#
# llama.cpp's libllama-common.so and libllama-server-impl.so need libssl.so.3
# and libcrypto.so.3. Fedora 45 and later ship OpenSSL 4 and keep 3 as the
# separate package openssl3-libs, which the .rpm depends on but nothing can
# install for an AppImage or a ZIP: there the engine did not load at all.
# Those two carry these two libraries in openssl3/, and gobbonet-launch uses
# them only when the dynamic loader cannot find the system's own. The .deb and
# the .rpm never carry them.
#
# The package is Ubuntu 22.04's, the system b10456 is built on, so the engine
# gets the OpenSSL it was linked against; it needs glibc 2.34, the AppImage's
# floor. Its hash was taken from jammy-updates' Packages index, whose own hash
# is in the InRelease file signed by the Ubuntu Archive Automatic Signing Key
# (2018), checked with gpgv against ubuntu-archive-keyring.gpg; jammy-security
# lists the same file. Plain http, as apt uses it: the hash is what is trusted.
# Moving to a newer build means the same check and all five values together.
OPENSSL3_DEB=libssl3_3.0.2-0ubuntu1.30_amd64.deb
OPENSSL3_DEB_URL=http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/o/openssl/libssl3_3.0.2-0ubuntu1.30_amd64.deb
OPENSSL3_DEB_SHA256=d1b4636e32ac6d3b95d583ac05ac548b1aa248414bae1c51b14f54be0f8fd7bc
LIBSSL3_SHA256=51fc92556f11ddce62f3f988d3fe973fab8fb4742032e61a713688581c924262
LIBCRYPTO3_SHA256=7cc817ff1841b59516d684f357bc0c3fc2cc52c3fa9b4ffb8ce8bdc215f02915
